{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/publications/firing-times-for-kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges","content_id":"df883eb3-e718-4434-bd49-33a49a14e5b4","description":"Firing times information for Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek.","details":{"attachments":[{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9572460","isbn":"","title":"Firing times for Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek Ranges October 2026","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/firing-times-for-kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges/firing-times-for-kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges"},{"attachment_type":"html","command_paper_number":"","hoc_paper_number":"","id":"9572461","isbn":"","title":"Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek Ranges firing times November 2026","unique_reference":"","unnumbered_command_paper":false,"unnumbered_hoc_paper":false,"url":"/government/publications/firing-times-for-kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges/kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges-firing-times-may-2026"}],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><div class=\"call-to-action\">\n  <p>Do not enter the danger area when the range is in use, this is a danger to life. Learn more about <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safe-access\">accessing MOD training areas safely</a>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>The only right of way available for use by the public on the range complex is via the bridle path.</p>\n\n<p>Maps are located at the following locations:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>beginning of the bridle path near the entrance to Whittington Village</li>\n  <li>the access point in the south of Hopwas Wood at the point of the bridge crossing the canal</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Members of the public must follow the route of the bridle path and not enter the range complex. Full details are contained within the <a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/staffordshire-byelaws\">Whittington byelaws</a>.</p>\n\n<p>Hopwas Wood and parts of the range may be used by soldiers for dry training, including the use of blank ammunition. Members of the public should stay on the bridleways or recognised tracks and observe any warning signs displayed.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/firing-notice\">UK military firing times for all ranges</a></li>\n  <li><a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/public-access-to-military-areas\">Public access to military areas</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"Added Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek November firing times.","public_timestamp":"2026-10-29T15:59:03Z"},{"note":"Added Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek Ranges October firing times.","public_timestamp":"2026-09-24T16:08:22Z"},{"note":"Added Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek September firing times.","public_timestamp":"2026-08-28T13:21:25Z"},{"note":"Added Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek August firing times.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-28T15:45:35Z"},{"note":"Added Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek July firing times.","public_timestamp":"2026-06-25T14:50:30Z"},{"note":"Added June firing times for Kingsbury, Whittington and Leek.","public_timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:12:56Z"},{"note":"Added Kingsbury, Whitington and Leek Ranges May firing times.","public_timestamp":"2026-04-30T12:54:41Z"},{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-31T10:45:00Z"}],"document_type_label":"Guidance","emphasised_organisations":["73068a99-7122-4cad-a876-35ca0b0778b4"],"featured_attachments":["9572460","9572461"],"first_public_at":"2026-03-31T11:45:00.000+01:00","political":false,"tags":{"browse_pages":[]}},"document_type":"guidance","first_published_at":"2026-03-31T11:45:00+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/publications/firing-times-for-kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/publications/firing-times-for-kingsbury-whittington-and-leek-ranges"